.TH SPINDLE-CONFIG-HELPER 1 "October 2026" "Spindle 0.13" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
spindle-config-helper \- generate and validate Spindle configuration files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spindle-config-helper
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spindle-config-helper
is a utility for generating and validating Spindle configuration files.
It parses configuration from command-line options, environment variables, and
existing configuration files, then outputs the resulting configuration in
.I spindle.conf
format.
.PP
In future releases, this tool will also probe the runtime environment to
automatically detect optimal configuration settings, including:
.IP \(bu 2
Local mount points suitable for cache and communication paths
.IP \(bu 2
Available resource managers (Slurm, Flux, LSF)
.IP \(bu 2
Security subsystems (Munge availability)
.IP \(bu 2
MPI environment characteristics
.PP
The tool is designed to be run on compute nodes in the same environment where
Spindle will execute, as login/front-end nodes may have different characteristics
than compute nodes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-usage
Display a brief usage summary with all available options and exit.
.PP
All Spindle configuration options are accepted. Use
.B --usage
to see a complete list of available options, or see the Spindle documentation
for detailed descriptions of each option.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Parse command-line options and output configuration:
.nf
.RS
spindle-config-helper --commpaths=/dev/shm --cachepaths=/tmp/cache
.RE
.fi
.TP
Parse an existing configuration file:
.nf
.RS
spindle-config-helper --config=/etc/spindle.conf
.RE
.fi
.TP
Combine multiple configuration sources:
.nf
.RS
export SPINDLE_SECURITY=none
spindle-config-helper --config=/etc/spindle.conf --launcher=slurm
.RE
.fi
.PP
The tool merges configuration from multiple sources in the following order
(later sources override earlier ones):
.IP 1. 3
Built-in defaults
.IP 2. 3
System configuration file
.IP 3. 3
User configuration file
.IP 4. 3
Environment variables
.IP 5. 3
Command-line options
.SH FUTURE FUNCTIONALITY
Future versions will support:
.TP
.B Environment Probing
Automatically detect and recommend optimal settings for cache paths, communication
paths, and other configuration based on the compute node environment.
.TP
.B Configuration Validation
Verify that specified paths exist, are writable, and are on appropriate filesystem
types (e.g., local vs. network filesystems).
.TP
.B Performance Tuning
Analyze the environment and suggest performance-oriented configuration settings.
.TP
.B MPI Integration
Run as an MPI application to gather environment information across all compute nodes
in an allocation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/spindle.conf
System-wide Spindle configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.spindle/spindle.conf
Per-user Spindle configuration file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. Valid configuration was parsed and output.
.TP
.B 1
Error. Invalid configuration or parse error occurred.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spindle (1)
